---
title: Angular
description: Keystone Dashboard Layout for Angular — in progress, reusing the same framework-agnostic core as the Vue package.
---

Angular support isn't published yet — this page exists so the landing
page's own framework picker doesn't link to a dead page while that's
in progress.

## What's already true

The positioning, collision, and compaction engine
(`@keystone-dashboard-layout/core`) is framework-agnostic by design —
built with zero Vue dependency specifically so an Angular (and React)
package could reuse it rather than reimplementing the same grid math
from scratch. See [Framework-agnostic core](/vue/features/#developer-experience)
on the Vue Features page for what that engine already provides.

## In the meantime

- **[Vue documentation](/vue/)** — fully complete: Guide, Components, API reference, and all 45 live examples.
- **[GitHub repository](https://github.com/gwinnem/keystone-dashboard-layout)** — check current progress, or open an issue.
